<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fire of Moscow (1812)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1812">1812</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as burning of Moscow</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> broke out in September 1812, shortly after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s army occupied the city. Much of Moscow was destroyed, depriving the French of shelter and supplies, and Napoleon was soon forced into a disastrous retreat. It became a symbol of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>'s resistance.</p></div>
